WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.130
2017 is shaping up to be a great year for
movies, with a ton of cool films already on

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.130
the schedule.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.740
In fact, so many great movies are coming out
next year, we thought you might need a jump

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:10.740
start on planning.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.610
Here's a look at the movies you won't want
to miss in 2017.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.269
Winter

00:00:16.269 --> 00:00:19.589
February was once the dumping grounds for
Hollywood's biggest failures.

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:23.730
But in 2017, the action heats up with the
long awaited big-screen adaption of Stephen

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.919
King's Dark Tower series, starring Idris Elba
as the iconic Gunslinger.

00:00:27.919 --> 00:00:29.519
How awesome is that?

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:34.550
And if that wasn't enough, the dark knight
returns once again with the Lego Batman Movie.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.880
Maybe this time he can finally save his parents.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.880
"Where's the seat belt?"

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.120
"The first lesson is, life doesn't give you
seat belts!"

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.540
Spring

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.770
In March, you can look forward to Kong: Skull
Island, which brings the legendary ape forward

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.070
into the 1970s for a showdown with Samuel
L. Jackson and Tom Hiddleston.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.420
Meanwhile, superhero fans will get the next
installment in the seemingly neverending series

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.500
of X-Men films with yet another Wolverine
flick.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:05.059
But the biggest film of the spring is undoubtedly
April's Fast 8, which reunites everyone's

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:10.310
favorite multi-cultural team of rebels with
an equally sleek and sexy array of fast cars.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.999
American filmmaking at its absolute peak!

00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:14.999
Summer

00:01:14.999 --> 00:01:20.530
In May, Marvel's hotly anticipated space romp
Guardians of the Galaxy volume 2 sets the

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:25.920
tone for a summer of fantastic sequels, including
follow ups for Pirates of the Caribbean, World

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.959
War Z, Kingsman, Transformers, Cars, and Despicable
Me.

00:01:29.959 --> 00:01:34.200
But they're all overshadowed by the June arrival
of Wonder Woman, which finally brings one

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.439
of the world's greatest superhero to the big
screen in the movie event of the year.

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:42.640
DC's film efforts have a pretty poor track
record with the critics so far, but Wonder

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.649
Woman looks like it may finally change all
that.

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:46.679
Awesome.

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:48.639
So does Marvel have an answer for Wonder Woman?

00:01:48.639 --> 00:01:50.719
Of course: it's your friendly neighborhood
Spider-Man.

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:54.310
"I'd love to keep this up but I've only got
one job here today and I've gotta impress

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.680
Mr. Stark, so, I'm really sorry.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.049
Ah!"

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:04.060
July's Spider-Man: Homecoming is the first
Spidey film produced by Marvel Studios as

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.110
part of their shared cinematic universe, so
it will be interesting to see how it plays

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.110
out.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:12.740
And if you're feeling burnt out on superhero
films and sequels, don't worry, because July

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:17.420
also brings legendary director Christopher
Nolan's gritty new war drama Dunkirk.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.420
Fall

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.250
In August, Ridley Scott returns with the newest
piece of the Alien universe with Alien: Covenant,

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:28.280
which, despite its title, is actually a sequel
to 2012's Prometheus.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.920
And another Ridley Scott sci-fi epic gets
a sequel with the follow-up to 1982's Blade

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:33.920
Runner.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.470
Nobody has any idea what to expect from it,
but whether it's awesome or a total train

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:40.220
wreck, you definitely won't want to miss it.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.450
Holidays

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:47.000
Three massive blockbusters anchor the 2017
holiday movie season, so you know exactly

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.250
what to ask Santa for next year.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.430
November starts with the release of Thor:
Ragnarok, which also features the Hulk.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:57.330
November continues with DC's answer to the
Avengers, Justice League.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:02.320
"I've heard about you, didn't think you were
real."

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.350
"I'm real when it's useful."

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:08.690
But as big as both of those movies are guaranteed
to be, both will be dwarfed by the December

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:15.340
15 release of one of the most highly anticipated
films of all time, Star Wars: Episode VIII.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.050
Will Luke actually talk this time?

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.620
We can't wait to find out.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:19.620
Thanks for watching!

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.260
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.640
And leave us a comment to let us know which
movie you're looking forward to most in 2017…

